<title>CANADA: Hollinger extends Southam bid.</title>
<headline>Hollinger extends Southam bid.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hollinger Inc said on Tuesday it extended its offer for the shares of Southam Inc it did  not already own and waived conditions to allow it to take up any shares of the newspaper chain tendered to the failed bid.</p>
<p>The C$23.50 a share bid to take Southam private failed on Monday night after only about six million or 15.6 percent of minority Southam shares were tendered to Hollinger's offer. A condition of the bid required at least 66.67 percent of minority shares to be tendered for the bid to succeed. Under the amended offer, Southam shareholders have until July 7 to tender to the bid.</p>
</text>
